@aid_reviewed_by claude-opus-4-7
@layer 2
@aid_version 0.2
@purpose Tokenizes Aria source into a stream of typed tokens with accurate position tracking, delimiter-aware newline insertion, and support for complex literals (hex/oct/bin integers, floats with exponents, duration/size suffixes, escaped + interpolated strings), enabling a single-pass parser with no backtracking.
@depends [diagnostic]

---

@workflow tokenize_pipeline
@purpose Source text -> token stream, single pass, no backtracking
@steps
  1. tokenize() creates a mutable Lexer state via new_lexer(source, file) [src: lexer.aria:588, lexer.aria:63]
  2. Main loop iterates character-by-character using _peek() + _advance() [src: lexer.aria:591-861, lexer.aria:81, lexer.aria:98-113]
  3. Dispatch to type-specific scanners (_scan_ident, _scan_number, _scan_string_impl, _scan_raw_string, operator/punct) [src: lexer.aria:591-861]
  4. Accumulate tokens via _add_token() with precomputed name field [src: lexer.aria:115-131]
  5. Delimiter depth counters (paren/bracket) suppress newline tokens inside balanced delimiters [src: lexer.aria:596-601, lexer.aria:151-152]
  6. String interpolation: on \{ branch to nested expr, resume via _scan_string_impl(is_continuation=true) after } closes [src: lexer.aria:448-459, lexer.aria:824-828]
  7. Diagnostics accumulate in DiagnosticBag; lexer never halts on first error [src: lexer.aria:133-149, lexer.aria:424-425]
  8. EOF token appended; immutable Lexer returned [src: lexer.aria:864-866]

---

@invariants
  Position is always in [0, source.len()); _peek() returns "" at EOF rather than panicking. [src: lexer.aria:81-86, lexer.aria:96]
  Token list always begins with a sentinel EOF token created at init; real tokens start at index 1. [src: lexer.aria:70, lexer.aria:115-131]
  line/col stay synchronized with pos after every _advance() / _newline(); col resets to 1 on newline. [src: lexer.aria:98-112, lexer.aria:202-216]
  Delimiter depth counters never go negative — decrements are guarded by > 0 checks. [src: lexer.aria:805-807, lexer.aria:815-817, lexer.aria:831-833]
  Interpolation depth + interp_brace_depth are saved/restored so the closing } can disambiguate interpolation-end from a literal brace. [src: lexer.aria:457-458, lexer.aria:781-792, lexer.aria:824-825]
  Keyword matching is case-sensitive — `fn` and `Fn` are NOT the same. [src: token.aria:263-309]

---

@antipatterns
  Calling _peek() or _peek_next() past EOF without checking _at_end() first: returns "", which silently falsifies character predicates and corrupts tokenization. [src: lexer.aria:81-94]
  Consuming a literal newline with _advance() instead of _newline(): col is not reset, breaking every subsequent token's position. [src: lexer.aria:202-216, lexer.aria:594-602]
  Advancing past a delimiter without updating depth via _set_depth(): newline suppression drifts out of sync with actual nesting. [src: lexer.aria:799-822, lexer.aria:154-168]
  String interpolation without saving interp_brace_depth before entering the expression: the closing } cannot tell interpolation-end from a literal brace. [src: lexer.aria:457-458]
  Raw-string lookahead that checks `r` then `#` without verifying the character after the hash count is `"`: `r#identifier` mis-lexes as a raw string. [src: lexer.aria:607-614]

---

@fn tokenize
@purpose Main entry. Scans source and returns a Lexer with the complete token stream and accumulated diagnostics.
@pre source may be empty; file is the diagnostic filename. [src: lexer.aria:588]
@post Lexer.tokens contains at least one token (EOF); all errors recorded in Lexer.diagnostics; position/line/col valid for final EOF. [src: lexer.aria:864-865]
@complexity O(n) where n = source.len(); single-pass, no backtracking. [src: lexer.aria:588-866]
@thread_safety immutable — returns a new Lexer; no shared state. [src: lexer.aria:588-866]
@antipatterns Expecting tokenize to stop at the first lex error: it emits diagnostics but keeps scanning so downstream phases see a complete stream. [src: lexer.aria:424-425, lexer.aria:461-471, lexer.aria:857-859]

---

@fn _scan_number
@purpose Parses decimal / hex / octal / binary integers, floats (with scientific notation), and duration/size suffixes in one dispatch.
@pre _peek() is a digit and source is not at EOF. [src: lexer.aria:244-379]
@post Appends exactly one token — TkIntLit, TkFloatLit, TkDurationLit, or TkSizeLit — and advances past every digit/letter of the literal. [src: lexer.aria:244-379]
@complexity O(k) where k = literal length; early exit on first non-digit after the prefix. [src: lexer.aria:244-379]
@antipatterns Misreading `..` as a fractional part — the float path explicitly checks _peek_next() is a digit after `.` before committing. [src: lexer.aria:290-309]
@antipatterns Ignoring `_` as a digit separator: each digit scan treats `_` as skippable. [src: lexer.aria:258, lexer.aria:267, lexer.aria:276, lexer.aria:285, lexer.aria:295]

