@fn _scan_string_impl
@purpose Core string scanner for both initial `"..."` and continuation after interpolation. Returns on `"` or `\{`.
@pre If is_continuation=false, _peek() is `"`. If is_continuation=true, the main loop just resumed after a `}`. [src: lexer.aria:407-480]
@post Emits TkStringLit (non-interpolated), or TkStringStart / TkStringMiddle / TkStringEnd around interpolation; interp depth counters updated on entry. [src: lexer.aria:450-459, lexer.aria:475-479]
@complexity O(m) where m = string length including escapes; single pass. [src: lexer.aria:407-480]
@antipatterns Expecting `\{` and `\}` to not need escaping: the scanner must escape them to avoid premature interpolation. [src: lexer.aria:440-443]

---

@fn _scan_raw_string
@purpose Parses `r"..."` and `r#"..."#` raw strings with matched hash counts so `"` and `\` pass through verbatim.
@pre _peek() is `r`; _peek_next() is `"` or `#`. [src: lexer.aria:607-614]
@post Emits TkRawStringLit; pos advanced past the closing quote and matching hash count. [src: lexer.aria:526]
@complexity O(m + h) where m = body length, h = hash count. [src: lexer.aria:504-525]

